# About this project

- This is my personal technical blog built with Astro.
- The site exists to publish articles that rank in search and stay useful to readers.
- A short About page covers who I am and how to contact me. There is no projects / case-study section.

# Design philosophy and technical details

- The frontend is implemented in the `src` folder. This is an Astro app based on the Astro blog template.
- This app uses a monochrome negative-space visual language: black, white, and soft greys; generous whitespace; Syne for UI display type; Libre Baskerville (print/newspaper tradition) for blog articles — while staying hand-coded CSS (no Tailwind).
- Blog posts use a multi-column newspaper layout on wide viewports, with italic/decorative typography treatments.
- I tried my best to ship zero JS to the client. Making the app performant and fast scoring 95+ on Google Lighthouse.
- The content management is done using Astro's markdown file based content management system. Blog posts live in `src/content/blog`.
- I am not using any tailwindcss for this project. In fact each component is hand-coded and styled. And there are some global styles declared in the `src/styles/global.css` file.
- The app is hosted on Vercel.
- Cross-surface branding is documented in **`public/design.md`**, served raw at **`/design.md`** (https://iswar.me/design.md). That guide uses the blog’s Libre Baskerville typography as the brand standard.
- **Required:** When changing this site’s UI or brand tokens, update `public/design.md` in the same change (see `.cursor/rules/design-system-sync.mdc`).

# Project structure

- `src/components` - Shared chrome (header, footer, head, date).
- `src/content/blog` - Markdown / MDX articles.
- `src/pages` - Routes: home, blog archive, about, RSS.
- `src/layouts/BlogPost.astro` - Article reading layout.
- `src/styles` - Global styles.
- `public/design.md` - Networked brand / design system (raw markdown at `/design.md`).
